cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use anchorprobe or the Stable Text Anchor profile, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "anchorprobe: Stable Text Anchor profile, drift forensics and conformance probes"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/klausbehnamshad/anchorprobe"
authors:
  - family-names: "Behnam Shad"
    given-names: "Klaus"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3601-9024"
    affiliation: "Luxembourg Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH), University of Luxembourg"
keywords:
  - web annotation
  - RFC 5147
  - CTS URN
  - Unicode normalization
  - text anchoring
  - digital humanities
  - research software
abstract: >
  An offset into a text is a measurement with a unit, taken on a particular encoding form.
  anchorprobe fixes both (code points, NFC, LF, no BOM), binds the anchor to a SHA-256 of
  the canonical text, maps it to W3C Web Annotation selectors, RFC 5147 fragments and CTS
  subreferences, explains deterministically why an anchor stopped matching, and probes
  running text services for how they count and hash.
